# INERT ON THE CURRENT HOST. This is Netlify / Cloudflare Pages syntax and
# GitHub Pages ignores it completely — GitHub sets its own cache headers and
# there is no way to override them from the repo. Kept because the caching
# intent below is correct and this file is what makes it one commit to move to
# a host that honours it. Do not "fix" a caching problem by editing this file
# while the site is on GitHub Pages; nothing here is being read.
#
# Cache-busting on GitHub Pages is the ?v= query on style.css / main.js in
# index.html instead — bump it when either changes.

/frames/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/main.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
